70 percent of patients at Olive View Medical Center in Sylmar rely on Medicaid for their healthcare.

Any cuts to Medicaid would be devastating to Olive View and the surrounding community, as it is also CA-29's largest employer.

@HouseDemocrats and I are fighting to protect Medicaid from any cuts.

As part of @HouseDemocrats' Medicaid Day of Action, I spoke with staff at Olive View Medical Center in Sylmar about how Republicans' cuts to Medicaid will impact the delivery of healthcare services.

Over half of my constituents rely on Medicaid, and many go to Olive View for healthcare.

@HouseGOP's Medicaid cuts will have a disastrous effect on communities across the country.

We are two days away from a Republican-led government shutdown and a worsening healthcare crisis.

An increase in healthcare costs and a lowering of coverage will make life harder for all the working families and individuals that rely on the services of these healthcare programs.

@HouseDemocrats are prepared to make a deal, but Republicans keep refusing to work with us to stop their reckless cuts to healthcare.

In less than 12 hours, Republicans will force the government to shut down and cause millions of Americans' healthcare premiums to soar.

Their shutdown will inflict harm on our most vulnerable.

@HouseDemocrats are in Washington ready to protect healthcare – but Republicans aren't even here to work for their constituents.
